# build output
dist/
# generated types
.astro/

# dependencies (no trailing slash so a node_modules SYMLINK is ignored too,
# not just the directory — a committed absolute-path symlink breaks CF builds)
node_modules

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*


# environment variables
.env
.env.production

# macOS-specific files
.DS_Store

# Internal operational documentation lives in a nested private repo at
# clawdemy/internal/ (gitignored below). The public CLAUDE.md in the repo
# root is editorial-discipline only; content-secret governance, Doc/*
# reference material, drafts/, and HANDOVER.md all live inside internal/.

# Playwright artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/

# Generated audio: regenerated from lesson MDX via scripts/generate-audio.ts.
# Master files will live in R2 once Phase 9.5 ships; for now we do not bloat
# the repo with binary MP3s that change every time a lesson is edited.
public/audio/

# MCP server configuration: local agent-link config, not part of the site.
.mcp.json

# Private internal repo (nested, gitignored)
internal/

# === Internals-are-internal recurrence guard (added 2026-06-24) ===
# Everything below is internal-governance or scratch that must never reach the
# PUBLIC repo. Each was previously untracked-but-addable: a stray `git add -A`
# would have committed it. Keep this block as the standing gate.

# Agent harness config (local permission allowlists, scheduled-task locks).
.claude/

# Nested private-repo working copies for the parallel-executor terminals.
# Each is its own clone of clawdemy-internal (CLAUDE.md, Doc/, drafts/,
# HANDOVER.md). They must never be embedded in the public repo.
clawdemy-internal*/

# Internal audit / backlog / handoff docs (track audits, currency checks).
audits/

# Founder Command Center docs. These four root entries are SYMLINKS into
# internal/command-center/, which is the private clawdemy-internal clone. They
# describe the content pipeline, the narration pipeline, the validators and the
# provider integrations: exactly the operational governance CLAUDE.md says is
# "intentionally not published here". The Command Center indexer reads the
# working directory and follows symlinks, so it finds them at the paths it
# expects while this public repo never carries them.
#
# ANCHOR EVERY PATTERN. A bare `docs/` would also match src/content/docs/ and
# silently hide all 1,858 lesson files.
#
# Audit note, because this has already been read as a hole once:
# `git check-ignore docs/decisions.md` prints nothing. That is a check-ignore
# limitation, not an exposure. It matches a path string against the patterns and
# does not apply the parent-directory prune that the real worktree walk applies.
# Two checks settle it, and both are run from the repo root:
#   git add -A --dry-run        stages nothing under docs/
#   git add docs/decisions.md   fails, "pathspec is beyond a symbolic link"
# Git never follows a symlink into a directory, so nothing under docs/ is
# reachable by any add. /docs with no trailing slash already covers the case
# where docs/ is replaced by a real directory, so no second pattern is needed.
/PRODUCT.md
/architecture.md
/backlog.md
/docs

# Trial + scratch artifacts (read-along trial audio, Playwright MCP scratch).
.read-along-trial/
.playwright-mcp/

# Loose scratch screenshots dropped at repo root during marketing/UI work.
# Legit site images live under public/ and src/assets/, never repo root.
/*.png

# This audit's own report is internal governance; never publish it.
/_governance-purge-report-*.md
